The animation wrapper uses `max-w-[280px]` for the open state, but ViewConfigPanel has its own fixed width (280px from the schema). This creates a tight coupling where the wrapper's max-width must exactly match the panel's internal width.

If ViewConfigPanel's width changes in the future, this animation will break. The wrapper also uses `overflow-hidden` which could clip content during the transition.

Consider using a more resilient approach:
1. Let ViewConfigPanel control its own width
2. Use `translate-x` transforms instead of `max-width` for smoother animation performance
3. Or apply the transition directly to the ViewConfigPanel component itself
```suggestion
                    className={`relative flex-none ${showViewConfigPanel && isAdmin ? 'w-auto' : 'w-0'}`}
                >
                    <div
                        className={`h-full transition-[transform,opacity] duration-300 ease-in-out ${
                            showViewConfigPanel && isAdmin
                                ? 'translate-x-0 opacity-100'
                                : 'translate-x-full opacity-0 pointer-events-none'
                        }`}
                    >
                        <ViewConfigPanel
                            open={showViewConfigPanel && isAdmin}
                            onClose={() => { setShowViewConfigPanel(false); setViewConfigPanelMode('edit'); }}
                            mode={viewConfigPanelMode}
                            activeView={activeView}
                            objectDef={objectDef}
                            recordCount={recordCount}
                            onSave={handleViewConfigSave}
                            onViewUpdate={handleViewUpdate}
                            onCreate={handleViewCreate}
                        />
                    </div>
